From: g2code33 <269358183+g2code33@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 29 Sep 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Add per-course and per-topic Export/Import for sharing
 questions between PharmaTRACK users

Every course header and every topic header in the Question Bank now has
its own Export and Import button:

- Export downloads a "PharmaTRACK question pack" (.json) — a course-wide
  export groups every topic's questions under that topic's name; a
  topic-level export is the same shape with a single group. Anyone can
  send this file to another student (email, WhatsApp, a USB stick,
  whatever) with zero server involvement.

- Import accepts either that pack format or the plain JSON array this
  app's existing global "Import JSON Bank" button already supported, via
  a file picker or paste. Importing at the topic level drops every
  question straight into that one topic. Importing at the course level
  matches each group's topic name to an existing topic in that course
  (case-insensitively) and creates a new one automatically when nothing
  matches, so a whole-course pack can be shared and land in the right
  place without the receiving student manually re-sorting anything.

New module `src/utils/questionShare.ts` holds all the pure pack-building,
parsing and import-planning logic (13 new unit tests in
`src/test/question-share.test.ts`); `QuestionBank.tsx` only wires it to
buttons and dispatches the resulting Topic/ExamQuestion records. The
existing global Import JSON Bank button and its modal are untouched.

Co-authored-by: arena-agent <297053741+arena-agent@users.noreply.github.com>
